Alembic — Nifty 50 Dashboard schema migrations

Source of truth
---------------
Post-baseline, alembic/versions/ is canonical for schema. sql/schema.sql is
the captured baseline (revision 0001_baseline) and is applied verbatim by
the baseline migration. Do not edit sql/schema.sql or add new
sql/migrations/*.sql — they will not be applied by ``alembic upgrade head``.

DB URL
------
alembic/env.py reads config.settings.db_url at import time. The
``sqlalchemy.url`` value in alembic.ini is a required Alembic placeholder
but is never used at runtime — set DATABASE settings via env vars / .env
the same way the rest of the app does.

First-time bootstrap on an existing database
--------------------------------------------
If your database already has the schema applied (via the old
``psql -f sql/schema.sql`` workflow), mark it as caught up to the
baseline without re-running DDL:

    alembic stamp 0001_baseline

Then ``alembic upgrade head`` will pick up any later revisions.

Fresh database
--------------
    alembic upgrade head

This creates every table in sql/schema.sql plus the alembic_version
tracking table.

Adding a new schema change
--------------------------
    alembic revision -m "describe the change"

Edit the generated file under alembic/versions/. Use ``op.execute(...)``
for raw SQL or the Alembic op DDL helpers. Then:

    alembic upgrade head
